# Line endings.
#
# Everything git recognises as text is stored with LF and checked out in the
# platform's own convention, except where a file only works one way:
#
#   .sh   bash reads a trailing CR as part of the command, so a CRLF script
#         fails outright on Linux and macOS. Keep these LF everywhere; Git Bash
#         on Windows reads LF scripts fine, and VSCodium's whole build is bash.
#   .bat  cmd.exe is the opposite case and expects CRLF.
#
# The VSCodium patches under vscodium/patches are deliberately left to the
# normal text handling: they are stored LF and applied to a checkout that git
# gave the same treatment, so the two always agree.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
